# Read-only database access for `npm run check`.
#
# Copy this file to .env.check (git ignores that one) and fill in the
# real string. Nothing else reads this file: it is not bundled, not
# deployed, and never printed -- scripts/check.mjs masks the password out
# of everything it writes, including the driver's error messages.
#
# WHERE THE STRING COMES FROM
#   Supabase -> Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string ->
#   "Session pooler" (the direct db.<ref>.supabase.co host needs IPv6).
#
# WHICH USER
#   Preferably the read-only login from
#   supabase/checks/PLAK-DIT-59-LEESACCOUNT.sql. If that plak reports it
#   cannot see past row-level security, use the postgres user instead --
#   the script still refuses everything but selects, and runs every
#   statement inside BEGIN READ ONLY ... ROLLBACK.
#
# NOTE THE USER NAME
#   Through the pooler the user carries the project reference after a
#   dot: psm_check.abcdefghijklm , not plain psm_check.
#
# If the password contains @ : / ? # or %, percent-encode it
# (@ = %40, : = %3A, / = %2F, ? = %3F, # = %23, % = %25).

CHECK_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://psm_check.abcdefghijklm:YOURPASSWORD@aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
